Parses three bracketed template operators that expand into stenographic output: `%[...]` repeats with optional separators, `%(...)` computed expressions, and `%<N>` end landings (cursor positions). These are dispatched from the parent template parser when a `%` is encountered.

`take_block_operator(n, acc)` routes on the character after `%` and delegates to the three parsers, advancing `self.i` by 2 to skip the opener. `parse_repeat()` calls `parse_chunks()` to extract segments, splitting on pipe (`|`) into separator and body if present, or treating the whole parse as an empty-separator repeat if no pipe is found. `parse_computed()` accumulates characters until `)`, hands the raw string to `super::super::expr::parse_expr()` for validation and AST construction, and fails if the expression doesn't parse. `parse_end_landing()` requires one or more ASCII digits between `%<` and `>`, parses them as `u32`, and rejects empty or non-digit content with specific error messages. All three return a `Chunk` enum variant that gets pushed into the accumulator. Parsing is character-by-character with `peek(0)` and manual index advance; no regex or other parsing combinator.